            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+equivariant+cohomology"} Borel-equivariant
            spectra are those which are
            %em right induced
            from plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+spectra"} equivariant spectra
            to plain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Schwede18"}> Schwede 18, Example 4.5.19
            )
          %h3#EquivariantWhitehead Equivariant stable Whitehead theorem
          %p
            The equivariant version of the stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
            holds:
          %p
            a map of
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon E \longrightarrow F
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            (e.g. an
            = succeed "-degree-wise" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RO(G)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
            in the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#IndexedOnAllRepresentations"} model via indexing on all representations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(f) \colon \pi_\bullet(E) \longrightarrow \pi_{\bullet}(F)
            on all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+group"} equivariant homotopy group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#GreenleesMay"}> Greenlees-May, theorem 2.3
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+category"} equivariant stable homotopy category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-grading"} RO(G)-grading
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spectrum"} fixed point spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+fixed+points"} geometric fixed points
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+sphere+spectrum"} equivariant sphere spectrum
          %h2#references References
          %p Good lecture notes are
          %ul
            %li#Blumberg17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/a.debray/lecture_notes/m392c_EHT_notes.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/adebray/equivariant_homotopy_theory"} GitHub
          %p
            The concept of genuine
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Gaunce+Lewis%2C+Jr."}> L. Gaunce Lewis, Jr.
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %p
            and in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            due to
          %ul
            %li#MandellMay04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "." do
                %em Equivariant orthogonal spectra and S-modules
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0408/"} KTheory:0408
          %p Further accounts:
          %ul
            %li#tomDieck87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
              , Section II.6 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Transformation+Groups"} Transformation Groups
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110858372"} doi:10.1515/9783110858372
          %p
            and in the context of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arf-Kervaire+invariant+problem"} Arf-Kervaire invariant problem
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hill"}> Michael Hill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doug+Ravenel"} Doug Ravenel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Arf-Kervaire invariant problem in algebraic topology: introduction
              %p
                %em> On the non-existence of elements of Kervaire invariant one
                , (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.3724"}> arXiv:0908.3724
                )
              %p
                %em> The Arf-Kervaire problem in algebraic topology: sketch of the proof
                , Current developments in mathematics, 2010, Int. Press, Somerville, MA, 2011, pp. 1–43
          %p Surveys and introductions include
          %ul
            %li#Carlsson92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
                ,
                = succeed ",Topology," do
                  %em A survey of equivariant stable homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/carlsson1.pdf"} pdf
            %li#GreenleesMay
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"}> John Greenlees
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} Equivariant stable homotopy theory
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
                , pp. 279-325. 1995. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/Newthird.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li#May96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                ,
                %em Equivariant homotopy and cohomology theory
                CBMS Regional Conference Series in Mathematics, vol. 91, Published for the Conference Board of the Mathematical Sciences, Washington, DC, 1996. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/alaska.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Schwede15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+Equivariant+Stable+Homotopy+Theory"} Lectures on Equivariant Stable Homotopy Theory
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Schwede18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Global+homotopy+theory"} Global homotopy theory
              2018 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.09382"}> arXiv:1802.09382
              )
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
          %ul
            %li#GuillouMay11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Guillou"}> Bert Guillou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                %em
                  Models of
                  = succeed "-spectra" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1110.3571"} arXiv:1110.3571
              %p
                %em
                  Permutative
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.3459"} arXiv:1207.3459
            %li#Nardin12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis+Nardin"}> Denis Nardin
                , section 2.6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stability and distributivity over orbital ∞-categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.univ-paris13.fr/~nardin/thesis.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Barwick14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spectral Mackey functors and equivariant algebraic K-theory (I)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1404.0108"} arXiv:1404.0108
          %p
            For more references see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            and at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functor"} Mackey functor
          %p
            Characterization via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+functors"} excisive functors
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Blumberg05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
              ,
              %em Continuous functors as a model for the equivariant stable homotopy category
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0505512"}> arXiv:math.AT/0505512
              )
          %p
            In the case of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            of prime order, genuine
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi hG
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi hG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{hG} \to E^G \to E^{hG}
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+Glasman"}> Saul Glasman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stratified categories, geometric fixed points and a generalized Arone-Ching theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.01976"} arXiv:1507.01976
          %p A perspective on the category of genuine G-spectra as a lax limit over those of “naive” G-spectra is given in
          %ul
            %li#AyalaMazelGeeRozenblyum17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ayala"}> David Ayala
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Mazel-Gee"} Aaron Mazel-Gee
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Rozenblyum"} Nick Rozenblyum
              %em
                A naive approach to genuine
                = succeed "-spectra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.06416"}> arXiv:1710.06416
              )
          %p
            Universal properties of the (∞,1)-category of genuine
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Bastiaan Cnossen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted ambidexterity in equivariant homotopy theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.00736"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                Tim Campion,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Free duals and a new universal property for stable equivariant homotopy theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04207"} arXiv
